# Welcome to the GX overview

GX is a domain specialised language to write array-based programs, including machine learning algorithms, data processing, or scientific programming. GX is designed to be embedded in a host language, Javascript and Go WASM for this website, and compiled at runtime.

Click on the Run button to execute the function named `Main`.

This overview is split into chapters, each chapter is composed of lessons. Access to the next lesson by clicking on the arrow below.

```code:main
package main

func Main() [2]float32 {
    return [2]float32{1, 2}
}
```

```code:options
{ "chapter_title": "Introduction" }
